WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.190 line:10%
 Being sick, losing your voice,

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.770 line:10%
as I did last week, it's good

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.180 line:10%
and it's bad.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.530 line:10%
It's bad because I couldn't be

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.370 line:10%
with you last Thursday

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.330 line:10%
and Friday.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.130 line:10%
But it's good because it gave me

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.780 line:10%
time to sit back and listen

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.580 line:10%
and watch.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.720 line:10%
I couldn't say anything,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.830 line:10%
at least for hours and hours

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.840 line:10%
and hours.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:18.960 line:10%
Now frankly, a lot of it

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.120 line:10%
was completely depressing

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.420 line:10%
and utterly predictable.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.630 line:10%
Now leave it to the Democrats

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.520 line:10%
to try to turn a virus that

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.370 line:10%
started mysteriously in China

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.380 line:10%
into a political attack

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.260 line:10%
against a US president.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.540 line:10%
 This question still remains

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.650 line:10%
whether or not the president

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.520 line:10%
gets it.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.410 line:10%
 The president is still just

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.570 line:10%
not being honest and upfront

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.960 line:10%
about the impact and the spread

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:44.760 line:10%
of corona.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.380 line:10%
Corporate America knows it is

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.180 line:10%
coming.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.380 line:10%
 You can't have

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.730 line:10%
an effective strategy to fight

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.110 line:10%
something if you won't

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.140 line:10%
acknowledge what it is

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:53.940 line:10%
that you're fighting

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.250 line:10%
and the risk that it poses.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.600 line:10%
 All the panic pushers,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.160 line:10%
they went into overdrive

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.410 line:10%
after the market closed.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.620 line:10%
It was a terrible day on Wall

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.460 line:10%
Street.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.349 line:10%
Now this is part of what was

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:05.970 line:10%
said in just a four minute

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.200 line:10%
period on CNN

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.210 line:10%
after the market closed.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.430 line:90%
 Investors are expecting

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.380 line:90%
a potential global recession

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.910 line:90%
because of the coronavirus.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.380 line:90%
So we've got all of this piling

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.450 line:90%
on as those worries

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.550 line:90%
and those fears.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.930 line:90%
And no one really knows what's

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:23.730 line:90%
going to happen

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:24.830 line:90%
with the coronavirus.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:25.830 line:10%
 Are things about to get even

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.630 line:10%
worse?

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.190 line:10%
 This virus is going to play

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.660 line:10%
havoc on the economic growth.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.640 line:10%
 There's a very good chance

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.500 line:10%
that we're headed into a US

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.920 line:10%
and global recession.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:36.720 line:10%
I mean, we have

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.370 line:10%
the perfect storm here.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.080 line:10%
 Let's just say that it was

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.630 line:10%
a series of, well,

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.340 line:10%
it's going into recession, well,

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.180 line:10%
it could fall further

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.140 line:10%
into recession.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.340 line:10%
No, it could be the worst.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.620 line:10%
It could be the perfect storm,

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.600 line:10%
one commentator said.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.460 line:10%
Well, a perfect storm with a lot

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.160 line:10%
of bluster and hot air.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.260 line:10%
Now even when Austan Goolsbee,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.550 line:10%
he pointed out

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.110 line:10%
an interesting possibility

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.700 line:10%
of an unusually fast market

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.720 line:10%
recovery.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:04.720 line:10%
Maybe in the summer,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.180 line:10%
things settle down.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.550 line:10%
Notice where CNN's Jake Tapper

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.870 line:10%
quickly took the conversation.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.100 line:10%
 There is one glimmer

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.360 line:10%
of optimism for a virus business

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.160 line:10%
cycle.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.570 line:10%
There is the possibility

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.250 line:10%
that this thing comes roaring

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.490 line:10%
back in a way

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.290 line:10%
that is not

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.390 line:10%
normal for a business

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.410 line:10%
cycle that's driven

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.410 line:10%
by other things.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.570 line:10%
 And then, Rhonda, let's talk

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:27.590 line:10%
about the travel and tourism

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:28.730 line:10%
industry because it's been hard

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.590 line:10%
hit hard by coronavirus.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.060 line:10%
We're showing some images now

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.170 line:10%
from northern Italy.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.490 line:10%
They're virtually empty ghost

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.720 line:10%
towns.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:36.900 line:10%
 Enough of that good news.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.300 line:10%
Let's go back to the bad news.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.730 line:10%
Italy, are you kidding me?

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.960 line:10%
Democrats don't even support

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.250 line:10%
locking down our own borders.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.200 line:10%
Now they're suddenly going

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.370 line:10%
to get on board with locking

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.610 line:10%
down entire US cities

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.410 line:10%
and towns-- what--

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.610 line:10%
with the National Guard?

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.970 line:10%
Oh, I can't wait to see the ACLU

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.770 line:10%
on that one.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.900 line:10%
Give me a break.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.460 line:10%
Now despite all this, the public

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.170 line:10%
in some ways seems a lot more

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.850 line:10%
level headed than all

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.300 line:10%
of the experts.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.200 line:10%
 68%, very or somewhat prepared

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.100 line:10%
if indeed somebody

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:06.940 line:10%
in their family gets

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.590 line:10%
coronavirus.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.140 line:10%
 Well, they're getting ready.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.610 line:10%
And the facts are actually

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:13.790 line:10%
pretty reassuring.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:14.890 line:10%
But you never know it watching

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:15.980 line:10%
all this stuff.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.780 line:10%
Now while the number

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.680 line:10%
of infected persons

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.287 line:10%
is more than 650 now--

00:03:19.287 --> 00:03:20.220 line:10%
the death toll has increased

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.020 line:10%
to 26--

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.210 line:10%
the risk to the average person

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.470 line:10%
does remain quite low.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.270 line:10%
We need to take care

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.140 line:10%
of our seniors.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.250 line:10%
If you're an elderly person

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.050 line:10%
or have

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.570 line:10%
a serious underlying condition,

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.205 line:10%
avoid tight, closed places,

00:03:31.205 --> 00:03:32.320 line:10%
a lot of people.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.180 line:10%
Don't take a cruise maybe.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.370 line:10%
Everyone else, wash your hands.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.340 line:10%
Use good judgment

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.540 line:10%
about your daily activities,

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.130 line:10%
yeah, pragmatic thinking,

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.360 line:10%
especially if you've been

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.470 line:10%
overseas recently in one

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.790 line:10%
of the hardest hit areas.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.950 line:10%
The president's coronavirus team

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.120 line:10%
is literally working

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.140 line:10%
around the clock to fight

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.760 line:10%
the epidemic spread

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.320 line:10%
and to give the public the most

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.400 line:10%
up to date information

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.480 line:10%
and guidance.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.650 line:10%
They should continue to have

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.600 line:10%
these no nonsense briefings

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.150 line:10%
to the press, preferably I think

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.680 line:10%
at the same time every day.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:01.700 line:10%
That would also be very

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.320 line:10%
reassuring.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.120 line:10%
Now as I said weeks ago,

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.100 line:10%
total transparency, even about

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.360 line:10%
the bad stuff,

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.530 line:10%
is going to go a long way

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.623 line:10%
to calm things down.

00:04:11.623 --> 00:04:12.590 line:10%
Public is going to know we're

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:13.460 line:10%
going to get through this.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.310 line:10%
We're America.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.230 line:10%
We do big things.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.570 line:10%
We get through tough stuff.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.500 line:10%
But apart from fighting

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.709 line:10%
the medical issues

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:22.010 line:10%
and the public health aspect

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.880 line:10%
of this nasty virus,

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.680 line:10%
there are four steps

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:27.050 line:10%
the president himself can take

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.820 line:10%
in an effort to protect America

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:29.630 line:10%
from sustaining

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:31.730 line:10%
deep economic wounds,

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.380 line:10%
steps by the way that hearken

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.180 line:10%
back to his original America

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.710 line:10%
first agenda.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.990 line:10%
Number one, immediately send

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.520 line:10%
your infrastructure proposal

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:41.810 line:10%
to Capitol Hill.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.100 line:10%
No more delays.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.047 line:10%
If the parties were working

00:04:44.047 --> 00:04:45.080 line:10%
in good faith, this should have

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.990 line:10%
happened years ago.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.000 line:10%
Call Pelosi and Schumer, bring

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.970 line:10%
him back to the White House.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.770 line:10%
No more drama.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.205 line:10%
No more pointing by Nancy

00:04:52.205 --> 00:04:54.100 line:10%
or running out or photo ops

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:54.950 line:10%
or running to the mics

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:55.750 line:10%
or the cameras.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.660 line:10%
Just get it and on.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.700 line:10%
Number two, this morning I wrote

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:00.660 line:10%
that the president should

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.090 line:10%
propose a temporary payroll tax

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.680 line:10%
cut for workers.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.773 line:10%
This afternoon it seemed

00:05:05.773 --> 00:05:06.840 line:10%
like the White House was reading

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.240 line:10%
my mind.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.740 line:10%
 Tomorrow we're seeing

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.540 line:10%
the Senate and discussing

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.520 line:10%
a possible payroll tax.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.750 line:10%
We're also going to be talking

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.120 line:10%
about hourly wage earners

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.520 line:10%
getting help.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.080 line:10%
 So the president is 100%

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.540 line:10%
committed that we will provide

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.160 line:10%
whatever tools we need.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.780 line:10%
 We're going to stand by those

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.430 line:10%
hardworking Americans and make

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.900 line:10%
it possible for us-- and put

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.980 line:10%
the health of America first.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.230 line:10%
 Yes, a targeted payroll tax

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.220 line:10%
cut will put more money

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.570 line:10%
in Americans' pockets,

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.770 line:10%
an important stimulus

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:40.730 line:10%
in rocky times.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.370 line:10%
Push the House Democrats to make

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.030 line:10%
this happen.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.720 line:10%
Number three, propose a new US

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.100 line:10%
industrial policy that's

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.680 line:10%
good for businesses and workers.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:52.730 line:10%
We need to get back to Made

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:54.650 line:10%
in America, especially when it

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.840 line:10%
comes to essential items that we

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.520 line:10%
cannot do without, like medical

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.470 line:10%
supplies, medical devices,

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.520 line:10%
prescription,

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.890 line:10%
and over-the-counter medicines.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:05.630 line:10%
China has a virtual monopoly

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.710 line:10%
on the ingredients used

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.480 line:10%
in antibiotics.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.040 line:10%
We should never have allowed

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.630 line:10%
that to happen.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.520 line:10%
It's time to decouple.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.170 line:10%
Incentivize companies to bring

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:17.660 line:10%
manufacturing back home.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.470 line:10%
We need to be less

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:19.880 line:10%
dependent on global markets

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.680 line:10%
and more self-sufficient.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:22.910 line:10%
This latest crisis makes

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.530 line:10%
the wisdom of Trump's America

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.450 line:10%
First agenda all the more

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.580 line:10%
compelling.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.350 line:10%
We can't keep flooding America

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.430 line:10%
with migrant families

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.880 line:10%
on the bogus asylum pretense

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:33.680 line:10%
either.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.670 line:10%
We gotta be stronger

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.930 line:10%
on these borders.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.580 line:10%
My final point--

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.480 line:10%
while some people are being

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:39.920 line:10%
flown back to Mexico pending

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.170 line:10%
their cases, thousands are still

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.100 line:10%
getting in, impossible to screen

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:44.900 line:10%
completely.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.340 line:10%
For health, you bet--

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.380 line:10%
it's impossible to do this.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.000 line:10%
Now is not the time for us

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.250 line:10%
to take in any extra burdens

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.540 line:10%
on our schools.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.800 line:10%
My son's schools, by the way,

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.150 line:10%
are closed all week

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:58.520 line:10%
in Montgomery County, Maryland.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.230 line:10%
We don't need any more burdens

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.750 line:10%
on the schools or the health

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.710 line:10%
care system.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:04.610 line:10%
And finally, although Trump

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.960 line:10%
can't order the Federal Reserve

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:06.950 line:10%
to lower interest rates--

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:08.210 line:10%
independent agency--

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:09.440 line:10%
we all should keep pressure

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:10.730 line:10%
on the Fed to do that.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.620 line:10%
Rates should be lowered.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.750 line:10%
Another stimulus needed, you

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.430 line:10%
bet.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.480 line:10%
If America enters

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.140 line:10%
a formal recession,

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:19.940 line:10%
well, Americans

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.710 line:10%
across every socioeconomic

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:22.970 line:10%
group, every age group,

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:24.530 line:10%
every ethnicity, every state,

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.080 line:10%
every county will suffer, many

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.190 line:10%
greatly.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:29.360 line:10%
If Democrats want to stand

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.160 line:10%
in the way

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.640 line:10%
of these commonsense measures,

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:32.440 line:10%
let them

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:33.290 line:10%
go to their constituents

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.480 line:10%
and defend that move.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.785 line:10%
Look, bad things happen.

00:07:36.785 --> 00:07:38.960 line:10%
And this virus is one of them.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.000 line:10%
But setting off panic

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:41.870 line:10%
around the world

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.590 line:10%
is not the answer.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.380 line:10%
We need to calm everything down,

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.570 line:10%
propose smart legislation.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.530 line:10%
We'll help do that.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.330 line:10%
Now think about this.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.800 line:10%
If Trump day after day

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:52.970 line:10%
is saying that he has a plan

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.530 line:10%
